{{- /*
  jira/link-bead — canonical bead↔JIRA linkage invariant, split into the two
  phases every caller already separates with a comment-mirror loop in
  between: the create-time linkage flags, and the `jira_updated` high-water
  mark commit. Extracted per mitto-w8jp.2 from sync-tasks Step 5A (create)
  / Step 5D (commit) and pull-issue Step 6.9 (commit); the new "JIRA: push to
  new" prompt is a second `create` caller.

  Callers pass a dict:
    "Phase"  — "create" or "commit". Required.
    "Target" — the bead-id placeholder text the caller's surrounding prose
               uses (e.g. "<id>" for the sync-tasks batch loop, or
               "{{ $target }}" for a per-bead prompt). Required.
    "Key"    — the JIRA-key placeholder text (e.g. "<KEY>" or "<key>").
               Only used by "create". Optional, defaults to "<KEY>".

  Usage:

      {{ template "jira/shared/link-bead" (dict "Phase" "create" "Target" "<id>") }}
      ...caller's own `bd create`/`bd update` command, and the comment-mirror
      loop, happen here...
      {{ template "jira/shared/link-bead" (dict "Phase" "commit" "Target" "<id>") }}
*/ -}}
{{- $phase := .Phase -}}
{{- $target := .Target -}}
{{- $key := "<KEY>" -}}{{- if .Key }}{{ $key = .Key }}{{ end -}}
{{- if eq $phase "create" -}}
Link the new bead to its JIRA ticket so the rest of the JIRA suite (`JIRA: pull issue`,
`JIRA: push issue`, `JIRA: sync tasks`) can find it again — whether via `bd create`'s
own `--external-ref`/`--labels` flags or a follow-up `bd update {{ $target }}`:

- Set `external_ref` to `jira-<key-lower>` — the **lowercase** JIRA key prefixed
  with `jira-` (e.g. key `{{ $key }}` → `external_ref = "jira-{{ Lower $key }}"`,
  concretely `jira-abc-123` for `ABC-123`). This is the exact form `JIRA: push issue`
  Step 1 and `JIRA: pull issue` Step 1 parse back out — strip the `jira-` prefix and
  uppercase the remainder to recover the JIRA key.
- Add the **`jira-sync`** label — the single gating label the whole JIRA suite (pull,
  push, sync) checks before touching this bead.

Do **not** write `metadata.jira_updated` at this point — see the "commit" phase
below; writing it now would poison the very idempotency guard it exists to provide,
since the body and comments have not been mirrored yet.
{{- else if eq $phase "commit" -}}
**High-water mark — commit `jira_updated` last.** Only after the body update and
every per-comment mirror append have both succeeded for this ticket, advance the
idempotency guard:

```bash
bd update {{ $target }} --set-metadata jira_updated="<ticket.updated>"
```

If either the body update or any per-comment append failed, **skip this write** —
leaving `jira_updated` behind lets a future run retry the missing pieces. Never
advance `jira_updated` past unmirrored data: bumping it early poisons the "already
up to date" short-circuit, so a missed comment becomes permanently unreachable
until some other JIRA event ticks `updated` again.
{{- end -}}
